      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "I'll read the original test and the CUT source to understand what's being tested.Now I understand the test. It verifies that:\n1. `withoutFeature()` on a default `Value` produces a distinct `Value` (the feature is explicitly disabled vs. not set)\n2. Equality is asymmetric in the expected sense (both directions return false)\n3. Neither value has a non-default radix\n\nLet me write the improved version with clear names, descriptive structure, and no unnecessary abbreviations.The improved test compiled successfully. The refactored version renames the test method to `test_withoutFeature_producesValueNotEqualToOriginal`, uses descriptive variable names (`defaultValue`, `valueWithFeatureDisabled`), removes unused imports, and adds brief comments explaining why `withoutFeature()` on an empty value creates a non-equal result — making the intent immediately clear to any reader."
    }
